<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i-1)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the above assertion seems to have a mistake in the logic. The correct assertion should check that the element at the current position in the old list is moved to the next position in the new list, starting from the insertion point. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index < i && i <= \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This ensures that for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the current position in the old list is moved to the next position in the new list.
