However, there seems to be a misunderstanding in the interpretation of the comment. The correct interpretation should be that for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element was null or equals the old element at that position. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index < i && i <= \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This ensures that starting from the index right after the insertion point, each element is the same as it was before the insertion.
